From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:34:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: qcom: matisse3g: retain boot framebuffer resources

The inherited framebuffer has no consumers for the MDSS clocks, power
domain or DSI supplies. On SM-T531 the early console disappears during
resource handover, while the kernel continues running through USB ACM.

Describe its resources using the existing simple-framebuffer interfaces.
The DSI supply mapping is confirmed in the SM-T531 revision 02 vendor DT.
Keep the common Matisse description unchanged and retain the bootloader's
mode; this does not enable the native DRM display pipeline.

Tested on SM-T531: MDSS remains on, the framebuffer holds its clocks and
supplies, and the owner observes continued display output beyond the
previous failure point. A brief blue transition during handover remains.
MicroSD I/O failures are a separate unresolved limitation.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
@@ -87,3 +87,19 @@
 &modem {
 	status = "disabled";
 };
+
+&framebuffer0 {
+	clocks = <&mmcc MDSS_AHB_CLK>,
+		 <&mmcc MDSS_AXI_CLK>,
+		 <&mmcc MDSS_BYTE0_CLK>,
+		 <&mmcc MDSS_MDP_CLK>,
+		 <&mmcc MDSS_PCLK0_CLK>,
+		 <&mmcc MDSS_VSYNC_CLK>,
+		 <&mmcc MDSS_ESC0_CLK>,
+		 <&mmcc MDSS_MDP_LUT_CLK>;
+	power-domains = <&mmcc MDSS_GDSC>;
+
+	vdda-supply = <&pm8226_l4>;
+	vddio-supply = <&pm8226_l5>;
+	vddiol8-supply = <&pm8226_l8>;
+};
-- 
